# Round cflra: the load path overlaps NVMe, host conversion and card upload (cflow load L1, L3, L4).
# The term is the card upload's wall, `load phases` upload_s, of one V4.1 start on a plan with a host set
# (plan (a), A6000), the model file evicted from the page cache first (the cold start). Decomposition
# [derived from the cflow audit's load notes and their measured rows]: the
# base binary's card upload reads its file bytes through the load thread's and the pool's page faults,
# 0.85-2.7 GB/s on a cold file against the 6.83 GB/s the host set's populate gets from the same drive
# (rig-log plan-triage.md:2062); the new binary reads the next segments ahead on 16 helpers (window 1 GiB,
# chunks 8 MiB), so the drive is the bound: upload rate 4.5-6.8 GB/s. Upload wall = bytes / rate, so the
# ratio new / base is (1.0..2.7) / (6.8..4.5): 0.15..0.60 at the band's corners, and 0.22..0.40 at its
# centre pairing (base 1.3 [23.2 GB in 17.3 s, derived from the 47.2 s cold start] against new 3.3-5.6).
# The same sitting prints the whole `load phases` line, so the cold wall (47.2 s base [measured, int039bat
# g-gate-ds41-load.log]; predicted 33-37 s after, with the host set's walk now beside the upload) and
# the restart wall (10.2 s base [measured]; predicted 5.4-7.3 s after) are read from the same rows without
# a second sitting; only upload_s is the card's term.
kind: ab
question: does reading the next card segments' file pages ahead of the copy (and the host set's walk
  starting beside the context and upload) take the V4.1 cold start's card upload from the faulting
  rate to the drive's?
term: `load phases` upload_s @ one start of generate_ds41, V4.1 plan (a), A6000, model files evicted
  from the page cache before each start, CARD_DONTNEED at its default - (new - base) / base, paired by round
unit: %
predict: -78..-60
rounds: 3
sd: 8 % assumed: a cold drive read's spread between runs; no cold-start repeat is recorded, and the
  band's near edge is 60 %, so the ruler does not decide the card
condition: tools/ref/load-ab.sh under the lease runs the base binary (a worktree at ca0a535df, generate_ds41
  built by cargo oxide in its own remote dir) and the new binary alternating, the order rotated every round, after
  one discarded start per arm; each start is stopped at its `load phases` record; before each timed start every
  shard of the model file is dropped from the page cache (posix_fadvise DONTNEED on each; mincore reads under 1 % of
  its pages resident, else the start fails by name, rc=evict) and the row records majflt, pgpgin and `Cached` from
  /proc/meminfo over the start; no row [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]
decide-in: land the three changes; open R9 (the restart's card drop on a plan with no host set) and
  R10 (the tier card's upload beside the main card's) on the new rate
decide-below: faster than the drive's 6.83 GB/s is not possible: the eviction did not take (Cached
  at start, majflt near 0): redo the eviction before reading any row
decide-above: the upload did not reach the drive's rate: read /proc/vmstat pgpgin over the upload
  against the plan's card bytes (the helpers read them) and perf the pool's memcpy with -e cpu-clock
  before any change; the bound is then the staging memcpy or the barrier per 32 MB piece, not the read
